{
    "Description": {
        "Id": "starsystemdef_Clayrock",
        "Name": "Clayrock",
        "Details": "Clayrock is like Mars, but bigger, with Earth-like gravity, yet with a part-near-vacuum and part-dust atmosphere of non-breathable crabon dixoide and iron, with plenty of weather.  It's also well-populated, with extensive shops and markets, with products of nearly any industry.  Many mechwarriors can be found in it's hiring halls, and the planet is something of a cultural center, well-known for where a lot of big things are in it's large cities.  Like other star systems in the area, it is under the control and ownership of The Federateed Suns, unless you ask a local group of terrorists that illegally call themselves a local \"government\" with no authority to do so as they attempt a civil war and try to overthrow House Davion's control of the star system, with much futility.  Regardless, they are an annoyance, and The Federated Suns work with the MRB in this area to stomp out the rebellion.  When spending time here, Clayrock offers a good amount of work for any mercenary group of mechwarriors who are willing to fight rebels for some decent cash.  Clayrock is famous for it's culture, clubs, and downtown cities and marketplaces, which more than make up for the lack of scenery, and non-existant wilderness and wildlife.  Stepping outside the cities, you need a space suit in the first place, and will find red soil dust dunes and winds swirling around, kicking up iron-rich dust, and not a single blade of grass.  Watch out for parts of dead bodies in a few places where the rebels shed a lot of blood - they don't decompose very well in the atmosphere, not to mention the lack of bugs and vermin that one would find on a planet with breathable air and life.",
        "Icon": ""
    },
